{
    desc => q{Ctrl-b scrolls viewport backward one full page},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/scrolling/ctrl_b_page`

Tests that `Ctrl-b` scrolls the viewport backward (up) by one full page.
The buffer has 40 numbered lines so a full page scroll is clearly visible.

Keys: `G` then `Ctrl-b`

- **ctrl_b_page_initial.png**: Cursor at line 1 col 0 on "scroll line 1".
- **ctrl_b_page_at_bottom.png**: After `G`, cursor at line 40 (last line), viewport scrolled to show bottom of file.
- **ctrl_b_page_after_ctrl_b.png**: Viewport scrolled backward one full page; cursor moved toward top of visible area.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('G');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('at_bottom');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('Control-b');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_ctrl_b');
    },
}
